RPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBATA DAISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBATA, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flywheel, wherein a first inertia body (2) is linked to a second inertia body (5) rotatable relative to an input member (2) of the first inertia body through a plurality of dampers (6) disposed in circumferential direction, a boss member (17) connected to the second inertia body (5) is installed relatively rotatably to the first inertia body (2), shafts (43, 37) extending generally in the same axial direction corresponding to the dampers (6) are installed in the first inertia body (2) and the boss member (17), respectively, both ends of the dampers are linked to the shafts (43, 37), respectively, and the second inertia body (5) is connected to the boss member (17), whereby the flywheel capable of easily performing a damper mounting operation can be provided.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un volant d'inertie fait d'un premier corps inertiel (2) relié à un second corps inertiel (5) rotatif par rapport à un organe menant (2) du premier corps inertiel (2) par l'intermédiaire d'une pluralité d'amortisseurs (6) disposés selon le sens du cercle. Un bosselage (17) relié au second corps inertiel (5) est disposé relativement rotatif sur le premier corps inertiel (2). Des goujons (43, 37) disposés généralement tous dans le sens de l'axe en regard des amortisseurs (6) sont montés, les uns dans le premier corps inertiel (2), les autres dans le bosselage (17). Chacune des extrémités des amortisseurs est reliée, selon le cas, à l'un ou l'autre des types de goujons (43, 37). En outre, le second corps inertiel (5) est relié au bosselage (17). L'invention permet la réalisation d'un volant d'inertie doté d'une fonction d'amortissement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>